   "summary": "The report argues that Japan has substantial armament stocks and access to raw materials, but shipping losses and limited processing capacity constrain expansion. Its opening sections estimate shipping and rail capacity, oil and steel output, other raw materials, and electric power. It then examines food and clothing rationing, fuel, housing, health and black markets. The final pages in this section assess armament production and the limits imposed by alloy steel quality, precision machine tools and tooling skills; the report continues beyond page 413.",
